"Nathan Lark is an Earth-born man from the Sol system, a graduate student in biology."
"On Earth he lived for labs and lectures in engineering biology and liked extreme sports."
"He nearly became a physicist and knows biology, chemistry, physics, astronomy and calculus."
"He is six and a half feet tall, and he once feared heights."
"His body holds no magic, and magic-resistant alchemical ingredients permeate his bones and brain."
"Prophecy cannot see him and Davrar cannot predict his outcomes; he is beyond fate."
"In the week this season opens, Taeol dho Droxol summons him naked into a tower west of Giantsrest."
"Taeol sought one of receptive mind with expertise in science, pushing the bounds of knowledge."
"Taeol forces the Giantsrest tongue into his mind with one painful spell, [Ankiko Rurkiuko]."
"Taeol offers him magic for Earth's scientific secrets, and Nathan resolves not to serve him."
"Davrar judges him at a Disadvantage, with no Talents, and speeds his growth."
"He breaks Taeol's [Memory Purge] in one night and rises from level 1 to 3."
"He takes High-tier Magic Resistance as his first Talent and declines Resolute Mind."
"He gains Focused Mind and Earnestness; Taeol threatens to put his soul in a golem core."
"Taeol's [Disintegrate] takes his left arm; he breaks Taeol's nose and knee with his fists."
"Taeol teleports away, and Nathan takes the Antimagic Brawler class at level 15."
"He leaves a drawing on his cell wall and words carved in a table, and sprints down the tower."
"He escapes the guardian golems into the pine forest and meets Vhala's Gemore scouts there."
"Later, he goes to Gemore and becomes an Adventurer who fights with his fists."
"Later, a self-healing Talent regrows his lost arm; it grows into his Immortal Body Talent."
"Later, the elk-centaur Artha teaches him to embrace rage against mages, and Artha dies."
"Later, he befriends Stella, Sarah, Aarl and Khachi of Gemore; together they are the Heirs."
"Later, the Heirs swear an oath on the Gemore Seal to defend Gemore and end the Endings."
"Later, Kia kicks him off the Gemore Seal's mountain, which starts his airwalking."
"Later, Taeol hires a team of Gemore Adventurers to kidnap him, and the attempt fails."
"Later, the Heirs clear the tomb of Sklias, and a Kalis tower dungeon nearly makes him a goat."
"Later, Litcliff's rulers try to kill the Heirs, and Stella burns its palace."
"Later, the mercenary Maelstrom takes a contract against the Heirs."
"Later, he fights a fire elemental in a pass above Halsmet and learns of wizardry from it."
"Later, he is trapped in Halsmet, hunted by Giantsrest mages."
"Later, Faline of the Assassins of Gemore teaches him her trade; their romance burns him."
"Later, he gains a second class for stealth and disguise, Spellslayer."
"Later, he kills Taeol days after Badud sets the two of them up as rivals."
"Later, he frees Halsmet's slaves, drives out Exea dha Humal, and cripples the archmage Hibril."
"Later, his antimagic keeps his memory through Badud's [Reverse Time] outside Halsmet."
"Later, Brox dies fighting Badud to shield him, and Gemore beats Giantsrest's army in a pass."
"Later, disguised as 'Natad' in Giantsrest, he and Faline kill Nol dho Chokiz to frame the Nails."
"Later, he kills innocents in Giantsrest to keep his secrets."
"Later, he charges alone into the Academy and frees the enslaved mind of its dungeon core."
"Later, he breaks wizardry, survives the Last Arrows of Olita and radiation, and fakes his death."
"Later, he kills Badud and cripples his automagic; Badud levels the Academy with its mages inside."
"Later, the Heirs free and rebuild Giantsrest, and he breaks thousands of slave collars."
"Later, he frees the slaves of the Chokiz district, among them the printers Thia and Shong."
"Later, Badud brings the Ending of History forward to strike Gemore within a century."
"Later, he suspects Davrar was built as a game for the Questors, and wants the Endings ended."
"Later, he leaves the continent by sea while Sussu and Ogarius send assassins after him."
"Years later, Eolinne's ship carries the Heirs to Keihona, where Sarya's grid trains them."
"His classes are then End of Magic, level 834, and Spellslayer, level 564."
"Sarya sets the Heirs' first deed: take Esebus by killing Badud's grid."
"He teaches Stella fusion and fission as an Insight, and swears the Heirs to keep it secret."
"In Esebus he kills three patrol soldiers, and Khachi kills Sussu in her vault."
"The Heirs loot Sussu's vault, then kill Badud, Ogarius and Amoh in Esebus."
"He guides Stella's hydrabane onto Ogarius; Sarah shoots Badud; Khachi raises the slain Stella."
"At level 729 his Spellslayer class becomes Death of Legends, on Sarya's advice."
"He carries the adamantium dagger that killed Syncarius, the one item he can hold unbroken."
"The Heirs sail to Helmaris, where Henrish of the Ashen Accord sets them to clear its Blight."
"He dives into the Blightmind and purges the Seal; his Talent becomes Magical Destruction."
"He can now drain a land's magic, strip a wizard's magic for good, and break Seals."
"He promises Stella not to destroy Seals, and wants mind magic removed from Davrar."
"Kaelis of the Ashen Accord cuts off his hand to test him; Aarl keeps the hand in stasis."
"In Ostren the Heirs fight a Polite War for the Ashen Accord against the Aleph Grid."
"In that war he kills Kamus of the gold tower and a wind-bodied Questor, and survives mincing."
"He earns the war's top contribution, 17.43 percent, and the Heirs win the right to a Conclave."
"At the Conclave in Dawn's Concord he gives the opening speech against the Endings."
"In Conclave duels he cripples Badud's magic, kills him a fourth time, and kills Kamus."
"Evesor's rod of annihilation vaporizes him, and he regrows from his stored hand."
"He strips Evesor's Questor link, then lets it return; his Talent becomes Davrar's Denial."
"He uploads his mind into Davrar to make the moral calls of the Continuance Charter, which passes."
"His body dissolves, and for months his friends see no sign of him."
"Nine years later, his influence seems to cancel the Severance Bloc's atomic spells."
"Eighty-one years later he walks as a tall young man in rough clothes, calling himself Davrar's soul."
"He then knows every Questor's name, can banish them from Davrar, and warns them off abusing mortals."
"At Sansal he throws the new Questor Eril skyward and strips his magic."
"Eighty-one years later he goes to a friend's hundredth birthday party."
